# Evaluation Metrics

This notebook records the current trajectory-evaluation metric suite and the
reasoning behind each metric. The goal is to avoid one blended score hiding
different prediction failures.

## Coordinate Convention

The model predicts normalized coordinates during training and inference. Before
evaluation, predictions and targets are converted back to MABe pixel coordinates.
All distance metrics below are therefore reported in pixels.

Mouse-local metrics use a body frame built from the actual mouse at the same
timestep:

```text
origin = center_back
forward_axis = normalize(tail_base -> neck)
lateral_axis = perpendicular(forward_axis)
```

Using the actual mouse frame asks where the prediction landed relative to the
ground-truth mouse position and heading.

## Primary Metrics

| Problem | Metric | Range | Better | Reason |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
| Mouse position over time | `centroid_ade_px` | `[0, inf)` | lower | Tracks global mouse trajectory without over-weighting individual keypoints. |
| Mouse final position | `centroid_fde_px` | `[0, inf)` | lower | Captures final rollout drift. |
| Keypoint position over time | `keypoint_ade_px` | `[0, inf)` | lower | Reference metric for full keypoint displacement. |
| Final keypoint position | `keypoint_fde_px` | `[0, inf)` | lower | Reference metric for final-frame keypoint displacement. |
| Signed horizontal offset | `centroid_x_offset_px` | `(-inf, inf)` | closer to 0 | Detects left/right centroid bias; positive means right. |
| Signed vertical offset | `centroid_y_offset_px` | `(-inf, inf)` | closer to 0 | Detects up/down centroid bias; positive means down. |
| Global body orientation | `body_heading_error_deg` | `[0, 180]` | lower | Checks whether the mouse faces the correct direction. |
| Semantic keypoint ordering | `relative_ordering_error` | `[0, 1]` | lower | Checks whether keypoints preserve pairwise front/back and side ordering. |
| Front/back ordering | `relative_ordering_error_forward` | `[0, 1]` | lower | Isolates ordering along the body axis. |
| Left/right ordering | `relative_ordering_error_lateral` | `[0, 1]` | lower | Isolates ordering across the body axis. |

## Diagnostic Tables

The CLI also prints Rich tables when evaluating a checkpoint:

| Diagnostic | Shape | Reason |
|---|---:|---|
| `centroid_offset_px_by_mouse` | `[3, 2]` | Finds signed x/y offset bias for each mouse. |
| `body_heading_error_deg_by_mouse` | `[3]` | Finds which mouse has orientation error. |
| `body_frame_keypoint_error_px_by_mouse` | `[3, 12]` | Finds which semantic keypoint is misplaced in the actual mouse frame. |
| `relative_ordering_error_by_mouse_axis` | `[3, 2]` | Splits ordering failures by mouse and body-frame axis. |
| `edge_angle_error_deg_by_mouse` | `[3, 12, 12]` | Locates pairwise shape / pose direction errors. |
| `edge_bone_length_error_px_by_mouse` | `[3, 12, 12]` | Locates body scale, stretching, or collapse errors. |

The pairwise matrices include all off-diagonal keypoint pairs. Diagonal cells are
ignored because a keypoint has no self-edge length or angle.

## Why These Metrics Are Not Redundant

- Centroid ADE/FDE measures global motion.
- Signed centroid offset measures directional bias, such as persistent rightward
  drift, which unsigned ADE/FDE cannot show.
- Heading error measures global orientation.
- Relative ordering error measures whether keypoints cross each other
  semantically, even when distances are small.
- Bone-length error measures scale and stretch.
- Edge-angle error measures pairwise pose direction.
- The per-keypoint body-frame table is diagnostic only. Its scalar ADE/FDE forms
  are omitted because using the actual mouse frame makes them equivalent to
  keypoint ADE/FDE under a shared rigid transform.

A model can score well on one and fail another. For example, it can predict the
right centroid while scrambling nose, ear, and tail ordering.

## Print Current Metric Contract

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python"}
metric_contract = [
    ("centroid_ade_px", "[0, inf)", "lower", "px"),
    ("centroid_fde_px", "[0, inf)", "lower", "px"),
    ("keypoint_ade_px", "[0, inf)", "lower", "px"),
    ("keypoint_fde_px", "[0, inf)", "lower", "px"),
    ("centroid_x_offset_px", "(-inf, inf)", "closer to 0", "px"),
    ("centroid_y_offset_px", "(-inf, inf)", "closer to 0", "px"),
    ("body_heading_error_deg", "[0, 180]", "lower", "degrees"),
    ("relative_ordering_error", "[0, 1]", "lower", "fraction"),
    ("relative_ordering_error_forward", "[0, 1]", "lower", "fraction"),
    ("relative_ordering_error_lateral", "[0, 1]", "lower", "fraction"),
]

for name, value_range, better, unit in metric_contract:
    print(f"{name:36} range={value_range:9} better={better:5} unit={unit}")
```

## Evaluation Command

```bash {"interpreter":"/bin/bash"}
python src/evaluate.py \
  --config src/config/dense_keypoint__train.yml \
  --test-config src/config/test.yml \
  --checkpoint checkpoints/dense_keypoint/flat_best.pt \
  --split test
```
